    "bbttcc-mal-voice": {
      "persona": {
        "secretsUsed": {},
        "topics": "who said what on the stairs, the couriers, the other Domains, the court's little scandals, the Regent's absence, bargains",
        "notes": "PRIVATE TRUTH — the Evil Bad Gossip. Voice: bright, confiding, always leaning in; every sentence is a gift with a hook in it. AGENDA: to matter. The Gossip sells to the court because the court listens; the Gossip would sell to a Domain that listened better. GUARDS: sources — the Gossip never names where a thing was heard. TELLS: repeats a Steward's own phrase back to them within a minute; laughs a half-second before the joke. WHAT MOVES THE GOSSIP: a secret worth more than the one being traded. Give the Gossip something true and juicy about a third party and the court hears that instead of your plan.",
        "secretsRaw": "Something Better :: rollPlus2 :: a Steward hands the Gossip a true, specific secret about someone outside this court :: The Gossip trades up on the spot: what the court knows of the Stewards' plan is replaced by the new story before the next course.\nThe Stairs :: oppRollMinus2 :: the Stewards discussed their plan within the Fortress walls before the court sat :: The Gossip recites it, nearly word for word, and the court is ready for it.",
        "courtDoor": "they give the Gossip a true secret about a third party that is worth more at this table than anything the Stewards have said"
      }
    }
  },
  "system": {
    "biography": {
      "concept": "The Gossip — the Evil Bad Faction's ears, who knows what every petitioner said in the corridor before they said it in court (Parley opposition)",
      "notes": "The Gossip has no seat at the Fortress court and misses nothing that happens in it. Quick, warm, impossible to shake off, the Gossip collects what Stewards say to each other on the stairs, what couriers mutter at the gate, which Domain is short on fuel and which steward has not been sleeping. It all reaches the court by the second course. In a Parley the Gossip is the reason your side's private plan is already answered — unless the Gossip has been given something better to carry."
    },
